# The Basics (otherAreas 6): its reply kinds against Event-priority competitors set by a GM, both before RQ7 in container
# order: Rycharde the Chef accepted (Rycharde 72, Take 68) and Expertise accepted at Prog 1 (Take 63, Valgeir 104). On a
# tie the lookup's action cycle plays the actions in container order, one per talk, from where it last stopped (a zone
# change clears it). Available: Rycharde's 94 (Progress: an Event 94 would tie and the cycle would play 72 first); not
# due: nil, 72 alone; Take's 66 (Event): 68, 63, 66; Valgeir's 144 (Event): 104, then 144. Accepted: Rycharde's 95
# (Event): 72, then 95; Valgeir's 106 (Progress: an Event 106 would play 104 first); Prog 1: 145 (Event): 104, then 145.
# Completed: Rycharde's 97 (Event): 72, then 97 (finished: the var cleared); then 98 (replaceDefault) loses to 72 every
# time; Take's 67 (replaceDefault) loses to 68 and 63 (68, 63, 68); Valgeir's 107 (Event): 104, then 107; then 146
# (replaceDefault) loses to 104. The trade reply (96 Progress) has no competitor.
lists Mhaura/Rycharde/onTrigger Mhaura/Take/onTrigger Selbina/Valgeir/onTrigger Mhaura/onEventFinish/94 Selbina/onEventFinish/106 Mhaura/onEventFinish/97 Selbina/onEventFinish/107
